# LinkedIn API Credentials Hook

# This hook provides LinkedIn credentials via injection
# The credentials are never stored in plain text in the vault
# Instead, they are securely injected at runtime

# The following environment variables should be available when this hook is used:
# LINKEDIN_USERNAME - Your LinkedIn username/email
# LINKEDIN_PASSWORD - Your LinkedIn password
# LINKEDIN_SESSION_COOKIES - LinkedIn session cookies for persistent login (optional)

# Instructions for setting up LinkedIn credentials:
# 1. Have a valid LinkedIn account with proper permissions
# 2. For persistent sessions, you may need to save cookies after first login
# 3. Store credentials securely in your system (not in this file)
# 4. Consider using 2FA-friendly approaches if your account has 2FA enabled

# This hook file is a placeholder - actual credentials should be
# injected via your secure credential management system.
# The skill will access these via environment variables or other secure means.

# Note: Be aware of LinkedIn's terms of service regarding automated posting